  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: json-smart 2.4.8.rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released net.minidev:json-smart 2.4.8.rhlw-00001 with a backported security fix.\n\nCVE-2023-1370: [Json-smart](https://netplex.github.io/json-smart/) is a performance focused, JSON processor lib.\n\nWhen reaching a \u2018[\u2018 or \u2018{\u2018 character in the JSON input, the code parses an array or an object respectively.\n\nIt was discovered that the code does not have any limit to the nesting of such arrays or objects. Since the parsing of nested arrays and objects is done recursively, nesting too many of them can cause a stack exhaustion (stack overflow) and crash the software.\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for net.minidev:json-smart 2.4.8 from Maven Central.",
